a) there exists an increasing sequence of positive real numbers, $(y_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$, converging to $0$, such that $y_n \le 2y_{f(n)}$, for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$;
b) if $(x_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ is a decreasing sequence of real numbers, converging to $0$, then there exists an increasing sequence of real numbers $(y_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$, converging to $0$, such that $x_n \le y_n \le 2y_{f(n)}$, for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$.

